elete/None)\n- 03 (all): back icon → 02_Welcome\n- 03_Filled: Create account → 04_Home\n- 04_Home: portfolio card → 05_My_Asset_Overlay (Open overlay? For overlay behavior, the 05 frame already contains home behind. Simplest: Navigation to 05 frame with animation \"Move in from bottom\" or \"Smart animate\". Since 05 contains home behind + sheet, Navigation with \"Move in (from bottom)\" looks right.) Actually brief says \"My Asset opens as an overlay above Home (not a separate pushed screen)\". With per-frame deliverables, Navigation → 05 with \"Move in from bottom\" animation conveys overlay. Or \"Open overlay\"? Figma prototyping: \"Change to\" / \"Open overlay\" only for overlay-style... In modern Figma there's \"Open over\" action? There's \"Open overlay\" for overlay flows where the target is an overlay in prototype. Simpler robust approach: Navigation action with \"Move in ← bottom\" animation. The evaluation checks \"flow & prototype completeness\" — links as listed. I'll use Navigate with Move In (bottom).\n- 04: notification icon → 06 (Navigate, slide from right? \"Move in from right\")\n- 04: Account tab → 07 (Navigate)\n- 05: close icon → 04 (Navigate, \"Move out — bottom\"?) Navigation back with \"Move out (down)\"... Figma animations: \"Move out\" isn't a nav animation; there's Smart animate, Dissolve, Instant, Move in, Move out (yes Move out exists for navigate back). I'll use Move out (down) for close, Instant for others where unsure. Keep it simple: Smart animate where geometry matches (close → 04), else Instant.\n- 06: back → 04\n- 07: Contact Info row → 08; Bank Account Info row → 09; Home tab → 04\n- 08: back → 07\n- 09: back → 07\n\nAlso maybe Home tab on 06/08/09? Not required. Keep to listed links (plus required tab behavior).\n\n**Component masters to create in workspace (\"My Components\" area):**\n1. `Btn / Secondary` (outline) — used for Login, See All Plans maybe\n2. `Btn / Disabled` variant? The provided button is a variant set \"Type=Pr