nk) + action (\"Change\"/\"Add\" primary semibold 15).\n\nCall 3: Build auth screens: 01_Splash, 02_Welcome, 03×3.\n\nCall 4: Build 04_Home.\n\nCall 5: Build 05 (clone home + sheet), 06, 07.\n\nCall 6: Build 08, 09.\n\nCall 7: Prototypes.\n\nCall 8+: Screenshots & fixes.\n\nPositioning: grid at (0,0), gap 60? Frames 414 wide: x positions 0, 474, 948, 1422, 1896. Row y: 0, 1032, 2064.\n\nComponents section: place at x=2500, y=0 with title. Masters spaced out.\n\nLet me now write Call 1 code. Keep helper functions compact. Note: plugin API in this environment: `figma.getNodeByIdAsync` (async), `figma.createFrame()`, etc. Also `figma.createImageAsync` is NOT supported. Image fills: clone existing rects to preserve images — for coins inside my PlanCard component, I'll clone node 5:37 (Plan_Coin_Gold rect) into the component. Cloning a rect with image fill is fine.\n\nFor Avatar_Neutral (5:27) it's a FRAME 150×150 radius 75 with fill — clone it and resize (need rescale? Resize frame → children scale? children keep absolute sizes; better use node.rescale(factor) if available — rescale exists on nodes: `node.rescale(scale)`. For avatar, resize frame to 96×96: children (silhouette image?) — let me check children of 5:27... The metadata earlier didn't show children (I limited depth). It's a frame with light green fill and probably an image inside. To resize safely, use rescale(96/150). I'll do that on clones.\n\nFont names: \"DM Sans\" styles: Regular, Medium, Bold. Inter: Regular, Medium, Semi Bold, Bold. Verify availability — loadFontAsync will throw if missing; wrap with listAvailableFontsAsync? That's heavy. Just try loading; if error, adjust.\n\nAlso note: The page name \"03 · Workspace\". Get page via `figma.getNodeByIdAsync('2002:2')`.\n\nSet page background maybe light gray for presentation? Not needed.\n\nLet me also plan the Splash more: green bg #31A062. White card 220×146 radius 24 centered (logo 180×119 inside, FIT). Also \"Paradise Invest\" wordmark below card? Not required. Keep: status bar white, home indicator white, logo card center, maybe subtle pattern circles. Auto-advance prototype: interactions on frame: `frame.prototypeStartNode`? Prototype actions: node `frame` with `frame.reactInterractions`... In plugin API: `node.reactInterractions` — actual API: `reactInterractions` property (typo in API) on nodes supporting interactions: `node.reactInterractions = [{trigger: {type: 'AFTER_TIMEOUT', timeout: 1200}, action: {type: 'NODE', destination: welcomeFrame, navigation: 'NAVIGATE', transition: {type: 'DISSOLVE', duration: 0.3}}, frames: {}}]`. Hmm the exact schema: Interaction { trigger: { type: \"AFTER_TIMEOUT\", timeout: number }, action: Action }. Action NODE: { type: \"NODE\", destination: node, navigation: \"NAVIGATE\"|\"SWAP\"|\"OVERLAY\"|\"CHANGE_TO\", transition: Transition, preserveState: boolean }. Transition types: { type: \"INSTANT\" } | { type: \"DISSOLVE\", duration } | { type: \"SMART_ANIMATE\", easing, duration } | { type: \"MOVE_IN\", direction, easing, duration } | { type: \"MOVE_OUT\", ... } | { type: \"SLIDE_IN\"...} | {type:\"SLIDE_OUT\"...} | {type:\"PUSH\"...}. \n\nFor on-tap: trigger { type: \"ON_TAP\" }? The API uses { type: \"ON_TAP\" }? I recall Trigger { type: \"ON_TAP\" } | { type: \"ON_HOVER\" }... yes ON_TAP exists. \n\nI'll write prototype code in a dedicated call and verify no exceptions.\n\nEasing: { type: \"EASE_OUT\" }, duration 0.3.\n\nOK. Also \"Currently selected nodes\" — fine.\n\nOne more consideration: the workspace page might need `page.setBackgrounds`? skip.\n\nText auto-resize: set textAutoResize = 'HEIGHT' or 'WIDTH_AND_HEIGHT' as needed; for ellipsis summaries use fixed width + truncation via 'HEIGHT' with maxLines? Plugin API: textTruncation = 'ENDING' with maxLines. Supported: `textTruncation` and `maxLines`. I'll set for article summaries maxLines 2.\n\nLet me write Call 1 now: setup + basic components (buttons, inputs, status bar white, home indicator white, nav bar).\n\nActually let me combine into fewer calls but stay under 50k chars. I'll write carefully.\n\nHelper functions I'll define at top of each call (functions don't persist between calls):\n\n```js\nconst P = await figma.getNodeByIdAsync('2002:2');\nawait figma.setCurrentPageAsync(P);\nconst F = {r:0x31/255,g:0xA0/255,b:0x62/255}; ...\nfunction solid(hex, op) {...}\nfunction txt(chars, font, size, hex, ls) { const t = figma.createText(); t.fontName=font; t.characters=chars; t.fontSize=size; t.fills=[solid(hex)]; if(ls)t.letterSpacing={unit:'PIXELS',value:ls}; return t; }\n```\n\nFonts must be loaded before setting fontName: `await Promise.all([...].map(f=>figma.loadFontAsync(f)))`.\n\nColors final:\n- ink: #18211C? Let me pick neutral-green-tinted grays:\n  - ink #16211B? I'll use #141B18 too dark? Use #1B2320 ink\n  - ink2 #5F6B64\n  - ink3 #98A29B\n  - border #E4E9E5\n  - divider #EEF1EF\n  - bg #F6F8F7\n  - surface #FFFFFF\n  - danger #D9483F? Use #E0473D... choose #DE5147? Let me use #E5484D.\n  - goldTint? not needed.\n- shadow effect: {type:'DROP_SHADOW', color:{r:0.05,g:0.12,b:0.08,a:0.08}, offset:{x:0,y:8}, radius:24, spread:0, visible:true, blendMode:'NORMAL'}\n\nButtons:\n- BtnSecondary: 354×60? For Login on welcome, full width 354. White bg, stroke border #E1E6E2 (1), radius 20, label ink Inter Semi Bold 17. Component `Btn / Secondary`.\n- BtnDisabled: primary bg at 45% opacity → compute blend on white: #31A062 at 45% ≈ #9BD0B1. Use solid #9BD0B1 with white label? Contrast poor but conveys disabled; label white 100%. Component `Btn / Disabled`.\n- Also small variant for \"See All Plans\" (Height 52)? Keep 60.\n\nInputs (my variants), all 354×60 radius 20 white:\n- `Input / Filled`: stroke #B7C2BB 1, text ink 17 Inter Regular, left padding 24? Reference: Value text width 307 in 354 → padding ~24 left. \n- `Input / Error`: stroke #E5484D 1.5, text ink, plus trailing? message separate.\n- `Input / Password`: stroke #B7C2BB, dots \"••••••••\" ink, trailing \"Show\" primary Inter Semi Bold 15 at right padding 24.\n\nNavBar component `Bar / Nav`: 414×56? width 414, transparent bg? Make width 354 content with back circle + title. Design: row: back icon in 40×40 tint circle? Keep minimal: back chevron icon (instance, ink) + title Inter Semi Bold 17 centered? For pushed screens: back left, title left-aligned next to back (common in this design style). I'll do left-aligned title after back icon, larger: DM Sans Bold 22? Hmm — iOS style: title centered 17. Design decision: back chevron left, title left next to it, DM Sans Bold 20. Component `Header / Pushed` with text override.\n\nTabBar component set: frame 414×84 bg white, top divider, 4 tabs each: icon (24 box) + label 11 Inter Medium. Active: primary color; inactive: #9AA39E. Variants: `Active=Home`, `Active=Account`. Icons: instances of icon components, recolored via override (set strokes/fills on all vectors). Tab icons: Home, Product Search, Transaction, Account.\n\nRecolor helper: `function paint(node, hex){ if('fills' in node && node.fills && node.fills!==figma.mixed && node.fills.length) node.fills = node.fills.map(f=> f.type==='SOLID'? {...f, color: hex}: f); if('strokes' in node && node.strokes && node.strokes!==figma.mixed && node.strokes.length) node.strokes = node.strokes.map(s=> s.type==='SOLID'? {...s, color: hex}: s); for(const c of ('children' in node? node.children:[])) paint(c, hex); }` — but careful: on instances, modifying nested children allowed (overrides). Setting fills on instance children is fine.\n\nHowever, for icons whose vectors use strokes only (e.g., Back has stroke), paint both fills+strokes. Some icons might have fills (Close has white x + gray circle). For Close, recolor circle to white? On overlay, Close icon (gray circle w/ white x) fine on white sheet.\n\nTabBar icons: instances inside component master; when I create variant masters separately, recolor accordingly (active tab icon primary, others ink3). Text label override per variant (Home