ld frames then `figma.createComponentFromNode(frame)` — that converts frame (in place) to component. Easier: build a frame f, then const comp = figma.createComponentFromNode(f). createComponentFromNode exists in plugin API. It keeps parent. Good.\n\nFor tab bar variants: build two frames, convert both, then combine into component set with figma.combineAsVariants([c1,c2], parent) and set names \"Active=Home\" etc. combineAsVariants(nodes, parent, index). Then set variant properties: the component set name \"Tab Bar\"; children names \"Active=Home\"/\"Active=Account\".\n\nFor instance creation: comp.createInstance().\n\nIcon instances: iconComp.createInstance() then paint() override, resize? Icons have intrinsic sizes (19×20 etc). I'll place at natural size mostly; tab icons ~20-25 tall — okay in 24 box, center manually.\n\nActually to simplify icon sizing: instance.resize(w,h) distorts? Vector scaling via resize scales geometry (rescale better). Use inst.rescale(target/original)? rescale exists on most nodes. I'll mostly keep natural sizes.\n\nLet me write the code now. Call 1:\n\n```js\nawait figma.loadFontAsync({family:'DM Sans',style:'Regular'});\n... Medium, Bold; Inter Regular, Medium, Semi Bold, Bold\n```\n\nNote: DM Sans may have \"Bold\" as style name. If not available, error — I'll handle in try/catch fallback to loading available styles? Keep simple; these fonts are standard.\n\nCode sketch (Call 1):\n\n```js\nconst page = await figma.getNodeByIdAsync('2002:2');\nawait figma.setCurrentPageAsync(page);\nfor (const f of [['DM Sans','Regular'],['DM Sans','Medium'],['DM Sans','Bold'],['Inter','Regular'],['Inter','Medium'],['Inter','Semi Bold'],['Inter','Bold']]) await figma.loadFontAsync({family:f[0],style:f[1]});\n\nconst C = {\n primary:{r:0x31/255,g:0xA0/255,b:0x62/255},\n primaryDark:{r:0x22/255,g:0x7C/255,b:0x4A/255},\n tint:{r:0xE7/255,g:0xF5/255,b:0xEE/255},\n tint2:{r:0xD6/255,g:0xEC/255,b:0xE0/255},\n ink:{r:0x1B/255,g:0x23/255,b:0x20/255},\n ink2:{r:0x5F/255,g:0x6B/255,b:0x64/255},\n ink3:{r:0x99/255,g:0xA3/255,b:0x9D/255},\n border:{r:0xE2/255,g:0xE7/255,b:0xE4/255},\n divider:{r:0xEE/255,g:0xF1/255,b:0xEF/255},\n bg:{r:0xF6/255,g:0xF8/255,b:0xF7/255},\n white:{r:1,g:1,b:1},\n danger:{r:0xE5/255,g:0x48/255,b:0x4D/255},\n grayStroke:{r:0x82/255,g:0x82/255,b:0x82/255},\n};\nfunction S(hex,op){const c={color:hex, type:'SOLID'}; if(op!==undefined)c.opacity=op; return [c];}\nfunction T(chars, fam, style, size, hex, op){const t=figma.createText(); t.fontName={family:fam,style}; t.characters=chars; t.fontSize=size; t.fills=S(hex,op); return t;}\nfunction frameWrap(name,w,h){const f=figma.createFrame(); f.name=name; f.resize(w,h); f.fills=[]; f.clipsContent=false; return f;}\nfunction shadowFx(node){node.effects=[{type:'DROP_SHADOW',color:{r:0.07,g:0.16,b:0.11,a:0.10},offset:{x:0,y:10},radius:30,spread:0,visible:true,blendMode:'NORMAL'}];}\nfunction paint(node,hex,op){ if('fills' in node && Array.isArray(node.fills)) node.fills=node.fills.map(f=>f.type==='SOLID'?Object.assign({},f,{color:hex,opacity:op===undefined?f.opacity:op}):f); if('strokes' in node && Array.isArray(node.strokes)) node.strokes=node.strokes.map(s=>s.type==='SOLID'?Object.assign({},s,{color:hex,opacity:op===undefined?s.opacity:op}):s); if('children' in node) node.children.forEach(c=>paint(c,hex,op)); }\n```\n\nWait: paint with fills mapping — for text with white fill to become green ok. But careful applying to icons with mixed fills... fine.\n\npaint on GROUP children: groups have children. OK.\n\nGetting icon comps: store dict: \n```js\nconst I = {}; for (const [k,id] of Object.entries({home:'6:269',search:'6:270',trans:'6:271',acct:'6:272',menu:'6:273',bell:'6:274',back:'6:275',chev:'6:276',close:'6:277',more:'6:278',edit:'6:279',contact:'6:281',funding:'6:282',bank:'6:283',doc:'6:284',set:'6:285'})) I[k]=(await figma.getNodeByIdAsync(id));\n```\n\nThese are COMPONENT nodes (masters). I keep references; cloning/instancing them doesn't modify them.\n\nStatus bar white: clone 48:43 component → figma.createComponent? A clone of a COMPONENT node via .clone() returns a COMPONENT (copy). Then paint to white, rename \"Shell / Status Bar (Light)\". Position in components area. But careful: clone of status bar: fill white already; recolor children (text + rects + battery) to white. The frame fill white → transparent? On green bg, the status bar frame's own white fill would cover bg! Set fills=[] on the clone (transparent bg), children white. Similarly home indicator clone: frame fill → transparent, rect white.\n\nDefault status bar (dark) usage: instance 48:43 directly has white bg fill — on white screens fine. But at top of screens the bg behind is white anyway. OK use instances directly.\n\nHmm wait: instance of 48:43: does instancing a master from another page work via createInstance? Yes.\n\nHome indicator dark: instance 48:54 on white screens.\n\nLayout coordinates for masters: \n- Section title at (2500, 0): \"MY COMPONENTS\" DM Sans Bold 24 ink.\n- Status bar light at (2500, 60); home indicator light at (2500, 120).\n- Btn/Secondary at (2500, 180); Btn/Disabled at (2500, 260).\n- Input/Filled (2500, 340); Input/Error (2500, 420); Input/Password (2500, 500).\n- Header/Pushed (2500, 580) 414×56.\n- Tab Bar set (2500, 660) 414×84 (two masters beside? combineAsVariants will stack them; set position after).\n\nRows etc in Call 2 at (2500, 800+) — I'll lay out as I go.\n\nNow, writing actual code. It's long; I'll try to be efficient but complete. Let me also decide Btn secondary width 354 h 60 radius 20.\n\nInput Filled component: frame 354×60 radius 20 white, stroke border(#E2E7E4)?? Earlier I said #B7C2BB; decide: stroke #DFE5E1 width 1 — too light vs reference gray #828282. Visual hierarchy: empty reference fields have #828282 stroke; filled fields usually calmer. I'll use #C7CFCA (between) for filled, error #E5484D 1.5. Text inside: x=24, vertically centered (use auto-layout? simpler: text y=(60-21)/2≈19.5). Use absolute positioning: t.x=24; t.y=20.\n\nPassword: value \"••••••••\" at x=24; \"Show\" primary at right: t.x=354-24-38≈292, y=20.\n\nError: same as filled but red stroke 1.5.\n\nHeader/Pushed: 414×56 transparent: back icon instance (paint ink) at x=30, y=17 (8×14); title at x=58, y=14, DM Sans Bold 20 ink. Text override per screen.\n\nTab bar: 414×84: white bg, stroke top? Use divider line rect 414×1 at top. Tabs: 4 columns each 103.5 wide; center icon box 24 at col center, label below at y=52 (Inter Medium 11). Positions: centers at 51.75, 155.25, 258.75, 362.25. Home icon 19×20 → x=center-9.5, y=18. Search 20×20 → x=center-10. Account 16×20 → center-8. Trans 25×25 → center-12.5, y=15? Keep icons vertically centered at y≈18-20.\n\nLabels: \"Home\",\"Product\",\"Transaction\",\"Account\"? Brief: tabs named Home · Product · Transaction · Account. Label \"Product\" (entry only). \n\nVariant Home: Home icon+label primary; others ink3. Variant Account: Account primary.\n\nI'll build function makeTabBar(activeIdx) returning frame; two masters.\n\nChevron rotation: chevron points up (16×8). To point right: rotation = -90. In Figma, rotation is counterclockwise positive; up chevron rotated -90 → points right? Up vector rotated -90° (clockwise) → points right. Yes rotation=-90. But rotation rotates around origin (top-left), causing position shift — after rotate, set x/y again to desired. I'll write helper placeRot(node,x,y,rot){node.rotation=rot; node.x=x; node.y=y;}\n\nOK, also all masters/components need names. After createComponentFromNode, comp.name='Btn / Secondary'.\n\nLet me now also confirm clone behavior for images inside component masters (Call 2): clone 5:37 rect → it lands in same parent; I appendChild into my master frame; set resize(56,56) — resize on rect with FIT scale: fits image, no stretch. Good.\n\nArticle thumbs 72×72 from portrait images with FIT → letterboxed? FIT scales image to fit within rect preserving aspect — for 106×160 into 72×72, FIT shows whole image with transparent bars top/bottom? scaleMode FIT = fit inside, may leave gaps. CROP = fill and crop. Guide says: \"use Fit for logos and coins, crop photos (articles, notifications) as needed. Do not stretch.\" So for articles/notifications: scaleMode CROP with imageTransform to cover. CROP requires imageTransform matrix (2x3). Setting scaleMode CROP with identity transform crops to top-left region? The imageTransform is the inverse mapping... Simpler: use scaleMode 'FILL'! ImagePaint supports scaleMode: FILL (like cover). Yes — 'FILL' fills rect cropping overflow. Use FILL for photos, FIT for logos/coins/illustration/bank logos. \n\nFor cloned rect: I set fills=[{type:'IMAGE', imageHash, scaleMode:'FILL'}]. Preserve bytes by reusing imageHash — allowed (hash references stored image). \n\nBank logos: FIT in 48×48 white rounded box.\n\nNotification thumbs: 48×48 FILL.\n\nWelcome illustration: 300×274 FIT natural size — no scaling issues.\n\nLogo: 240×159 FIT; on splash use width 190 → h 126 (keep ratio).\n\nAvatar: clone frame 5:27, rescale to 96 (rescale(0.64)). rescale multiplies children too. Then radius: 75*0.64=48 auto via rescale.\n\nNow Call 1 code. I'll write it now carefully. Also create the section title text.\n\nAfter building masters in call 1 & 2, verify by reading back (the call returns summary).\n\nOne risk: `figma.createComponentFromNode` on a frame with children — fine.\n\ncombineAsVariants: `figma.combineAsVariants(nodes, parent)` → ComponentSetNode. Set name 'Tab Bar'; children component names must be 'Active=Home' style. Then reposition set.\n\nLet me write Call 1.\n\nAlso: all created nodes appended to page (append to component masters' parent = page). createFrame defaults parent = current page. Fine.\n\nEdge: `t.textAutoResize` default WIDTH_AND_HEIGHT — ok for labels. For multiline fixed-width texts: set textAutoResize='HEIGHT' and resize width first? Order: create text, set characters, then `t.textAutoResize='HEIGHT'; t.resize(w, t.height)`. \n\nFor summaries with maxLines: t.textTruncation='ENDING'; t.maxLines=2.\n\nNow write the code. I'll produce Call 1 with: fonts, helpers, refs to icons, shell light clones, buttons, inputs, header, tab bar, section title. Return JSON summary of created ids (store mapping in return for later use!). Important: later calls need node ids of masters — I'll return an id map. \n\nLet me count size — will be ~8-10k chars. OK.\n\nAlso note the \"Currently selected nodes\" mention: irrelevant.\n\nOne more thing: `figma.createRectangle()` etc. Let me write.\n\nFor Btn/Disabled color: mix primary with white 55%: r=0.31+0.69*0.55... compute: white blend 0.55 toward white from primary: r=0.192+(1-0.192)*0.55=0.636, g=0.627+(0.373)*0.55=0.832, b=0.384+(0.616)*0.55=0.723 → #A2D4B9. Label white.\n\nInput filled stroke: #C9D2CC: r=0.788,g=0.824,b=0.8.\n\nHeader back circle: none; just icon + title.\n\nTab bar: also home indicator area separate — tab bar height 84 incl safe area? Put tab bar y=898-84-? Screen 932: home indicator 34 at bottom (898-932). Tab bar above it: y=814, height 84 → 814+84=898. Good: tab bar 414×84 with divider at top, icons centered in upper 50px, labels at y~50, bottom 34 padding region. I'll design tab bar frame 414×84: divider line y=0; icon boxes centered x, icon y=16; label y=46. \n\nWait icons vary in height (16-25). I'll set each icon y so that vertical center = 28: y = 28 - h/2. Label y=44 (11px → baseline area 44-57). Bottom empty 84-57=27. Good.\n\nHome indicator dark instance at y=898 on each frame; on splash use white clone.\n\nStatus bar: y=0.\n\nContent top starts y=44.\n\nWrite Call 1 now. Also include page rename? No.\n\nActually, also need `Btn / Primary Disabled` maybe used on Error + Empty. And `Btn / Secondary` for Login + See All Plans (See All Plans maybe smaller width — override width per instance fine).\n\nAlso add `Chip / Level` for \"Expert\"? Inline on profile, skip component.\n\nReturn map ids. Go.","signature":"9466ae411e5