= targetTop + h. targetLeft = inst.x + (rb.x-ri.x). Yes as written.\n\nAlso recolor on fresh instance OK.\n\nOne more concern: inst.findAll(n=>n.type==='INSTANCE')[0] — finds arrow inside badge. But badge itself is FRAME (not instance) containing arrow instance. ✓.\n\nBut also — will `arr.visible=false` work on instance child? Visibility IS overridable in instances. ✓.\n\nFor Sell rows: arrow stays green (default primary color) — default is primary already; fine, no recolor needed. But recolor default arrow is green ✓.\n\nAlso '06' avatar approach unchanged.\n\nAdditionally the profile recolor(inst.fills?inst:null) line — recolor(null) would crash: [null].concat → nodes includes null → n.fills throws → caught by try{}catch{} inside loop — actually nodes=[root] where root=null: nodes[0]=null, loop n=null → 'fills' in null → TypeError caught by try? The try wraps the fills checks — `'fills' in n` with n=null throws, caught. OK harmless. But let me clean: recolor on icon after swap to ensure primary color — the icon components already primary-colored? They're reference icons presumably black/gray. In master, bank icon was recolored primary at build? I built profileEntry with \"bank icon primary\". After swapComponent, new icon instance may inherit its own fills (black?). recolor(ic,C.primary) instead. Fix that line: recolor(ic,C.primary).\n\nWait but swap replaces nested instance inside Icon Box (inside the row instance) — can I recolor fills of instance children? Yes fills overridable; only transform/rotation not. ✓.\n\nAlso, chevron inside profileEntry instance is fine (already ink3 in master).\n\nRewrite and rerun full Call 5 with cleanup of partial '05_My_Asset_Overlay'.","signature":"2817afdf375544f0b2f251d9"}],"id":"e6a75d95-6c5c-4e74-82d9-d12f344c831d","model":"glm-5.3-flash","role":"assistant","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6