{"type":"assistant","message":{"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The property is `reactions` (with `setReactionsAsync`). Old-style API. Reaction structure:\n\n```ts\ninterface Reaction {\n  trigger: Trigger; // e.g. {type:'OnTap'} or {type:'AfterTimeout', timeout: number}\n  action: Action;   // {type:'NODE', destinationId, navigation, transition} etc.\n}\n```\n\nIn the REST/plugin v1 typings (older): \n- Trigger: {type: 'OnTap'} — note casing! Older API used {type: \"OnTap\"}, {type: \"AfterTimeout\", timeout}. \n- Action: {type: \"NODE\", destinationId: string, navigation: \"NAVIGATE\", transition: Transition}.\n- Transition: {type: \"DISSOLVE\", duration?: number} or {type: \"MOVE_IN\", direction: \"BOTTOM\"}? Older transitions: {type:'MOVE_IN', direction:'FROM_BOTTOM'}? Hmm.\n\nThe typings (figma-plugin-dts old):\n```ts\ntype Trigger = \n | { type: 'OnTap' } \n | { type: 'OnHover' } \n | { type: 'OnPress' } \n | { type: 'OnDrag' }\n | { type: 'AfterTimeout', timeout: number }\n | { type: 'KeyDown', keyCodes: number[] }\n ...\n```\nAnd Action:\n```ts\ntype Action =\n | { type: 'BACK' | 'CLOSE' | 'URL', url?... }\n | { type: 'NODE', destinationId: string | null, navigation: 'NAVIGATE' | 'SWAP' | 'OVERLAY' | 'SCROLL_TO' | 'CHANGE_TO', transition: Transition | 'INSTANT', preserveState?: boolean, overlay?: {...} }\n```\nTransition:\n```ts\ntype Transition = \n | { type: 'DISSOLVE' | 'SMART_ANIMATE' | 'MOVE_IN' | 'MOVE_OUT' | 'PUSH' | 'SLIDE_IN' | 'SLIDE_OUT', duration?: number, easing?: Easing, direction?: 'LEFT'|'RIGHT'|'TOP'|'BOTTOM' }\n | { type: 'SCROLL_ANIMATE', ... }\n```\nFor MOVE_IN, direction means where it comes FROM: 'BOTTOM'.\n\nAlso setReactionsAsync exists — reactions might be read-only getter with async setter! `setReactionsAsync(reactions)`. Given both `reactions` prop and `setReactionsAsync` present, try setting `node.reactions = [...]` directly; if read-only, use setReactionsAsync.\n\nNote: casing matters — older API used 'OnTap' (title case). If wrong, error will tell. Timeout: {type:'AfterTimeout', timeout:1200}.\n\nLet me write link():\n```js\nfunction link(node,dest,transition){\n  const rx=[{trigger:{type:'OnTap'},action:{type:'NODE',destinationId:dest,navigation:'NAVIGATE',transition:transition||{type:'DISSOLVE',duration:0.25}}}];\n  try{ node.reactions=rx; }catch(e){ node.setReactionsAsync(rx); }\n}\n```\nsetReactionsAsync is async — but if assignments throw we need await. Make link async and always try direct set first inside try; if throws, await node.setReactionsAsync(rx). Since whole script is in async context, fine.\n\nSplash: reactions=[{trigger:{type:'AfterTimeout',timeout:1200}, action:{...}}].\n\nRewrite Call 7 with reactions.","signature":"fc9ec6ff8e3d4a0d8666ac75"}],"id":"46d91ead-6cf1-46fb-8ca3-c0c0bf3dc6e5","model":"glm-5.3-flash","role":"assistant","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"613de0ee-9d26-413e-bccb-2a00f6a3efc8","uuid":"37f32d68-0b28-4664-8704-cd0dccb8713c","timestamp":"2026-10-28T19:56:22.133Z","thinking_duration_ms":13073}
